{
    "title": "Deepstash: Smarter Every Day!",
    "description": "<b>Learn something new in just 5 minutes</b>, with unlimited daily access to <b>200,000+ powerful ideas</b> from top books, articles, podcasts, videos and more, in just 4 easy steps:\r\n\r\nStop Scrolling Social Media \u21e8 Download Deepstash \u21e8 Use it for 5 min/day \u21e8 Become the smartest in the room.\r\n\r\nJoin 3 Million+ smart people to discover new ideas, learn new things, improve yourself and inspire others.\r\n\r\n<b>Knowledge</b> in Deepstash comes in the form of ideas, represented as little cards you can read at a glance. Ideas are short notes that condense profound thoughts into simple sentences. They could be: the best ideas from a book or article, inspiring quotes, practical tips on any topic. Each idea belongs to a topic, from #marketing to #leadership and #philosophy, which you can follow.\r\n\r\nIdeas are created by users just like you. Whenever you read a book, article or listen to a podcast and find a concept, a thought or quote that is worth saving, remembering and sharing, you can add an idea about it in Deepstash. You see the source of the idea right in your feed.\r\n\r\nWhat to do with ideas? They are fundamental to your wellbeing, success in life or your career. Ideas can make you:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Smarter</b> (you'll know more stuff, doh!)</li>\r\n<li><b>More Creative</b> (you can connect more dots)</li>\r\n<li><b>Happier</b> (better habits, less anxiety)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nIt's your daily source of inspiring & life changing stories and ideas. Read articles, learn skills, get productivity tips and discover life hacks. The magic of Deepstash is that everything you do builds your knowledge library: be it contributing  your own ideas or collecting idea cards from other stashers. Fuel your curiosity and get smarter daily.\r\n\r\n<b>Personalized content & feeds</b>\r\n\r\nChoose a few topics of interest and directions (like increasing productivity, building better habits or earning more money) and then just use Deepstash at your leisure. As you read and save ideas, we learn what you like and find the best stories, articles, books, podcasts and other top content to show you every day. You don\u2019t even have to work for it.\r\n\r\nThe more you read and save ideas the better we learn what articles and topics you love. We refresh your recommendations multiple times a day so you never run out of fresh ideas.\r\n\r\n<b>Build and organize your knowledge</b>\r\n\r\nYou can save ideas in your own profile and build your own library of facts, skills, quotes, information and ideas that matter to you and which you can use at any time.\r\n\r\nSearch and filter your ideas and organize your knowledge into personalized stashes, stocked up and ready to go for when you need them: a Powerpoint presentation, a new job interview, a date, a project at work, or negotiating your rent with the landlord.\r\n\r\n<b>Share your knowledge</b>\r\n\r\nAdd your own ideas and stash them in your knowledge library so you always have them at hand.\r\n\r\nShare your own or other ideas you find with your friends and colleagues on Whatsapp or Facebook or send it to your followers on Facebook, Twitter, Tiktok, Instagram, Linkedin or Quora. The Deepstash bite-sized idea format is great for this. \r\n\r\n<b>Why our users love Deepstash:</b>\r\n\r\n\"It helped me get off social media. So excellent to learn something, and I feel like the time I spent was valuable. I also spend about 10 minutes every morning picking a topic and enjoying it. Great app, well-done Kudos\" - Ron Ronald\r\n\r\n\"Even five minutes a day will improve your thinking. I've come across new ideas and learnt to improve existing ways to become more motivated, confident and happier.\" - Ghazala Begum\r\n\r\n<b>What the Media is buzzing about us:</b>\r\n\r\n\"Learn good habits, health practices, and more on your time. Makes personal growth manageable\" - Mashable\r\n\r\n\"More than 200,000 game-changing ideas at your fingertips\" - MacWorld\r\n\r\n\"Deepstash is perfect for entrepreneurs who want to stay updated but are short on time.\" -Entrepreneur.com\r\n\r\nGood for your career. \r\nGreat for your life. \r\nGive it a shot!",
    "descriptionHTML": "<b>Learn something new in just 5 minutes</b>, with unlimited daily access to <b>200,000+ powerful ideas</b> from top books, articles, podcasts, videos and more, in just 4 easy steps:<br><br>Stop Scrolling Social Media \u21e8 Download Deepstash \u21e8 Use it for 5 min/day \u21e8 Become the smartest in the room.<br><br>Join 3 Million+ smart people to discover new ideas, learn new things, improve yourself and inspire others.<br><br><b>Knowledge</b> in Deepstash comes in the form of ideas, represented as little cards you can read at a glance. Ideas are short notes that condense profound thoughts into simple sentences. They could be: the best ideas from a book or article, inspiring quotes, practical tips on any topic. Each idea belongs to a topic, from #marketing to #leadership and #philosophy, which you can follow.<br><br>Ideas are created by users just like you. Whenever you read a book, article or listen to a podcast and find a concept, a thought or quote that is worth saving, remembering and sharing, you can add an idea about it in Deepstash. You see the source of the idea right in your feed.<br><br>What to do with ideas? They are fundamental to your wellbeing, success in life or your career. Ideas can make you:<br><ul><br><li><b>Smarter</b> (you&#39;ll know more stuff, doh!)</li><br><li><b>More Creative</b> (you can connect more dots)</li><br><li><b>Happier</b> (better habits, less anxiety)</li><br></ul><br>It&#39;s your daily source of inspiring &amp; life changing stories and ideas. Read articles, learn skills, get productivity tips and discover life hacks. The magic of Deepstash is that everything you do builds your knowledge library: be it contributing  your own ideas or collecting idea cards from other stashers. Fuel your curiosity and get smarter daily.<br><br><b>Personalized content &amp; feeds</b><br><br>Choose a few topics of interest and directions (like increasing productivity, building better habits or earning more money) and then